<title>BANGLADESH: An opposition strike shut Bangladeshi bourses.</title>
<headline>An opposition strike shut Bangladeshi bourses.</headline>
<dateline>DHAKA 1997-07-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bangladesh's bourses - the main Dhaka Stock Exchange (DSE) and the Chittagong Stock Exchange - were closed on Thursday as an opposition-led eight-hour strike disrupted communications and businesses across the country.</p>
<p>Main opposition Bangladesh Nationalist Party (BNP) called the strike to protest imposition of higher taxes in the country's budget for fiscal 1997/98 which began on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The DSE all-share price index fell 13.2 points or 1.18 percent to 1,098.35 on Wednesday. The market will reopen on Sunday after the Friday-Saturday weekend in Bangladesh.</p>
<p>-- Dhaka Newsroom +880-2-506363</p>
</text>
